<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">2006 People's Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2006">2006</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Loktantra Andolan, Jana Andolan II, 2006 Nepalese revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 2006 People's Movement, also called Jana Andolan II, was a wave of general strikes and mass protests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in April 2006 against the direct rule of King Gyanendra. Organised by the main parliamentary parties in alliance with the Maoist insurgents, it forced the king to restore parliament after nineteen days. It opened the way to the 2006 peace agreement and the abolition of the monarchy in 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/2006-peoples-movement.jpg" alt="2006 People's Movement" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bardalimakamala9982 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arjun_Narasingha_KC_arrested_by_King_during_Nepal_Uprising.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
